<id/13/1377/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Turmeric"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_natural_dyestuffs/#concept> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_15048> ;
    skos:definition "a name for the tubers of the *Curcuma longa*, which are bitter and aromatic, and largely used in the East as an ingredient in curries. Turmeric is imported into this country as a dye-stuff, and used to colour butter. The colouring matter of the dried root is bright yellow. White paper, dyed by an alcoholic turmeric, is a very sensitive test for alkalies. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 404]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — source_taxon remove: Indian dill, unrelated to turmeric."@en ;
